# (build 168d) LANGUAGE changed on the select screen (NEW GAME /
# CONTINUE / ERASE GAME), which opens where the backup check's message
# window closed: the text window's place in the stack, which the ROM
# keeps. Until 168d a change of language there typed the check's last
# message again -- into the menu, over its words and lamps, the cursor
# left lit on a blank row (The owner: "the lines don't update quite
# right. The flashing red cursor floats over text with no perimeter
# box"). Now the menu is built again in the new language, as every open
# window is (build 166), and nothing is typed into it.
start new
wait screen title
wait idle
press start
wait screen intro
wait idle                   # NEW GAME / CONTINUE / ERASE GAME
expect script $130B         # "Let me check the backup data."
expect script $1310         # "Data check complete."
language retranslation
wait ticks 2
expect pixel 65 56 $EEE     # CONTINUE's lamp, its top edge (until 168d
                            # the window's blue: the check's message there)
shot 01_retranslated
language ja
wait ticks 2
expect pixel 65 56 $EEE
shot 02_japanese
press down
wait ticks 12
shot 03_japanese_down
language us
wait ticks 2
expect pixel 65 72 $EEE     # ERASE GAME's lamp, the cursor on CONTINUE
shot 04_english
